    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1331">

                <pb facs="1142" n="1038" xml:id="pg1038"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/530.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Minister.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 24, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your February 20. The bankers say they have cabled a proposition to Mr. Bundy
                    Cole and are very anxious for favorable action of the Assembly on option for
                    remaining 49% of the railroad.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
